# Copy to hooks/channel-ceiling.conf. Shared by two guards that watch the same shared
# files, so they only need configuring once:
#   - git-hooks/pre-commit's channel-file insertion ceiling: refuses a COMMIT that adds
#     more than LIMIT lines to one of these files in one go (a sign two sessions' entries
#     landed together).
#   - hooks/channel-size-guard.sh's hard stop: refuses further growth once a file's TOTAL size
#     crosses the hard stop — checked live, on every Write/Edit/MultiEdit/Bash-append, not only
#     at commit time. (The <band> column below is the size an edit may always end at or under,
#     and the "sweep down to" target in hooks/channel-size-post.sh's message; the guard prints
#     no note between band and stop, since stderr on an exit-0 hook is not read.)
#
# One optional LIMIT line (default 100, used only by pre-commit), then one line per file:
#   <repo-relative glob pattern>  [<unit> <band> <hard-stop>]
# The pattern is matched with a plain bash `case` glob — "NOTES.md" matches only a
# top-level file for pre-commit's ceiling, "*/NOTES.md" one in any folder. <unit> is "words"
# or "lines" (or "bytes"). Leave the last three fields off a line to add a pattern to
# pre-commit's ceiling ONLY — channel-size-guard.sh ignores a line with no unit/band/stop.
# A pattern can appear on more than one line with a different unit (a file watched on both
# its word count and its line count). channel-size-guard.sh (and its post-write companion)
# read a pattern like this: WITHOUT a slash it matches by BASENAME, so `NOTES.md` there means
# any file called NOTES.md; WITH a slash it matches the file's repo-relative path, so
# `docs/plans/NOTES.md` watches that one file and `*/NOTES.md` any nested NOTES.md (a top-level
# one needs its own `NOTES.md` line). Outside a git work tree there is no repo path, so the
# bare file name is compared with the pattern's own basename instead.
#
# No file at all: neither guard does anything for any file — the safe default for a repo
# with no shared files several people or sessions append to.
LIMIT=100
NOTES.md          words 9000 15000
CHANGELOG.md
*/NOTES.md        words 9000 15000
